# Play Test - TPLY (the plan's TPLAY: a NAME is five characters), a TEST course (SPEC.md 130.54.2): the
# BZDEV=1 build's alone, after the shipped courses (the Makefile's BZ_TESTCRS), on no pad, with no shipped
# demo.  "Physics and replays" (docs/plans/BOUNCE-BONANZA-SOAK.md): the home of the bonanzaphys,
# bonanzareplay and bonanzaring-ground scenarios that ran on the PROTOTYPES (FIRST, TRIAL, MOON, PEAK,
# PLAYGROUND), each feature a few steps from the start or from a poked cell.  Four parts:
#  - the APRON (PLAYGROUND's, at H's height): the start (19, 14) on a level 15 x 6 tier, its four RUNGS
#    along the back row (tops 2, 1.5, 1 and 0.5 units up, x 7 - 18, wy 9 - 11; approached along -wy from
#    the front row wy 17; ADJACENT, no apron between them: a 64-wide course has the width for no more),
#    and the BRAKE STRIP (lane wx 12, wy 18 - 20) off its front edge into a VOID over the well (14 - 15,
#    21 - 24: a floor 16 units down, so the fall is as long as PLAYGROUND's - the GLIDE `nosafe` and
#    `nolatch` arms need it);
#  - TRIAL turned a quarter (its +wx is +wy here; cell (Tx, Ty) -> (Ty + 8, Tx + 9)): H's LIP the apron's
#    front edge over F (18 - 21, 18 - 21, 6 units down), the 2-tile GAP, G (18 - 21, 24 - 27, 2 above F)
#    and its far rail, the STEEP ramp along +wx off G (2 units a tile, 4 tiles), the MAT beside its foot,
#    the turn, the ICE back along -wy between BUMPER rails, the SAND and the SPLIT GOAL (25, 17) exit 0,
#    (26, 17) exit 1 - the autopilot's route, as TRIAL's: off the lip, bounced over the gap onto G, down
#    the ramp, along the ice to exit 1 in 529 steps (9.7 s), no fall, both flags touched;
#  - the YARD (at the goal's height, off the turn): FIRST's PLATEAU (28 - 30, 31 - 33, 4 up) with its back
#    RAIL and its RAMP down along +wx to a 2-unit LIP onto a 3-column foot and the void past it; the PADS
#    (one of each ball); SPRING 1 (29, 35) two rows before the plateau's face, which throws rubber onto it,
#    and SPRING 2 (37, 30); a plain EAST wall (38, 28 - 29: the +wx edge test, TRIAL's G rail turned away
#    from it); the HOLE (26, 30) flag 0 rolls into;
#  - the STRIP (`box 2 6 70 98`, from the yard's foot down the screen): 14 cells of level ground along
#    +wx +wy, the drag's one-arrow (Down) run from rest to the axis model's top and from the cap back to it.
#  Two FLAGS on the route: flag 0 (26, 26) on the turn, rubber, the hole beside it; flag 1 (19, 26) on G,
#  glass.  A course with a flag (or a cup) respawns at the flag, never at bz_safe (GF_CKPT), so the SAFE
#  respawn is BENCH's, not this course's.  `limit 20`: a timeout is TQUIK's (8 s) to wait out.
course TPLY "Play Test"
test             # SPEC.md 130.54: a test course - no pad, no shipped demo, no target owed
music trial      # SPEC.md 130.50.3: every course names its song
width 64
ball rubber
uses spring
# the APRON (H, the start tier), its rungs, the brake strip and the well under its void
floor rect   7 12 22 18  flat 14
floor rect   7  9 10 12  flat 16              # the 2-unit top
floor rect  10  9 13 12  flat 15.5            # 1.5
floor rect  13  9 16 12  flat 15              # 1
floor rect  16  9 19 12  flat 14.5            # 0.5
floor rect  11 18 14 21  flat 14              # the brake strip, lane wx 12
floor rect  14 21 16 25  flat -2              # the well: the strip's void falls as far as PLAYGROUND's
# F, the gap, G and its far rail
floor rect  18 18 22 22  flat 8
floor rect  18 24 22 28  flat 10
wall  rect  18 28 22 29  flat 10.5
# the steep ramp along +wx off G, its inner rail, the mat beside its foot
floor rect  21 25 25 28  ramp x 21 25 10 2
wall  rect  21 24 25 25  flat 10.5
floor rect  21 28 25 30  flat 2
surface bounce rect 21 28 25 30
# the turn, the ice back along -wy between bumper rails, the sand, the split goal
floor rect  25 25 27 28  flat 2
floor rect  25 20 27 25  flat 2
surface ice rect 25 20 27 25
wall  rect  24 20 25 24  flat 2.5
wall  rect  27 18 28 28  flat 2.5
surface bounce rect 24 20 25 24
surface bounce rect 27 20 28 28
floor rect  25 18 27 20  flat 2
surface sand rect 25 18 27 20
goal  rect  25 17 26 18  flat 2
goal  rect  26 17 27 18  flat 2 exit 1
# the YARD: the plateau, the pads, the springs, the east wall, flag 0's hole; the drag's strip below it
floor rect  25 28 39 36  flat 2
floor rect  28 36 31 37  flat 2               # spring 1's footing (no void beside a spring)
wall  rect  38 28 39 30  flat 3               # the plain east wall
hole  tile  26 30
floor box    2  6 70 98  flat 2               # the drag's strip
wall  rect  28 30 31 31  flat 8               # the plateau's back rail, 2 units proud
floor rect  28 31 31 34  flat 6               # the plateau
floor rect  31 31 35 34  ramp x 31 35 6 4     # its ramp; the lip, 2 units, onto the foot (35 - 37)
pad rubber 30 29
pad steel  32 29
pad glass  34 29
spring 29 35 640                              # onto the plateau (PEAK's 768 throws rubber past it)
spring 37 30 512
checkpoint 26 26 ball rubber                  # flag 0, the turn
checkpoint 19 26 ball glass                   # flag 1, G
start 19 14
way 19 14
way 19 26
way 23 26
way 26 26
way 26 22
way 26 17
limit 20
clock 26 23                                   # the finish clock (SPEC.md 130.22.6), TRIAL's, off the route
